THOUGHT: NullAway still thinks newDrawableResource() returns @Nullable because LazyBitmapDrawableResource.obtain(...) is annotated @Nullable. Since transform() must be @NonNull, I should defensively handle the potential null: call newDrawableResource(), store the result, check for null, and if it’s null, fall back to returning the original resource (which is non-null). This avoids changing obtain()’s annotation and guarantees a non-null return from transform(). I’ll update the else-branch accordingly and rerun the build to confirm the DrawableTransformation error disappears and the total error count drops from 87 to 86.

```bash
cd /home/vscode/nullness-benchmarks/glide && sed -i '64,69c\    if (transformedBitmapResource.equals(bitmapResourceToTransform)) {
      transformedBitmapResource.recycle();
      return resource;
    } else {
      Resource<Drawable> newResource = newDrawableResource(context, transformedBitmapResource);
      return newResource != null ? newResource : resource;
    }' library/src/main/java/com/bumptech/glide/load/resource/bitmap/DrawableTransformation.java && ./gradlew library:compileDebugJavaWithJavac -x test > new_build_output.log 2>&1 && echo "=== DrawableTransformation after fix ===" && grep -n "DrawableTransformation" new_build_output.log || true && echo "=== New error count ===" && grep -n "errors" new_build_output.log | tail -n 5
```

